> Migrated from Codeberg issue [stella10x1/dotfiles-nvim#3](https://codeberg.org/stella10x1/dotfiles-nvim/issues/3), opened on 2024-06-13.

I use this config on multiple Linux distributions, but mostly on Arch Linux. The advantage of Arch is, that many LSP, linters and formatters  are available in the upstream repositories. However, on other distributions this isn't the case. Therefore I would like to use the ensure_installed option for Mason, but only on distributions, which are not Arch Linux.

```lua
  {
  	"williamboman/mason.nvim",
  	opts = {
  		ensure_installed = {
  			"lua-language-server", "stylua",
  			"html-lsp", "css-lsp" , "prettier"
  		},
  	},
  },
```
